---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

// Privacy policy for the "Automate" TikTok developer app.
//
// Required by TikTok's app review: the form will not accept a submission
// without a live privacy policy URL, and reviewers check that it describes what
// the app ACTUALLY does. The most-cited rejection reason is a mismatch between
// the submission and the live product, so this is deliberately written as a
// narrow, accurate description of a single-operator drafting tool rather than a
// generic template that claims more than the app does.
//
// Kept off the site nav on purpose: it is a compliance document for one
// integration, not a page the blog's readers need.

const updated = '2 September 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Automate"
  description="Privacy policy for Automate, a personal TikTok drafting tool."
>
  <main class="legal" id="main">
    <p class="eyebrow mono">AUTOMATE · TIKTOK INTEGRATION</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated mono">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <h2>What this covers</h2>
    <p>
      Automate is a private, single-operator tool used by May Abiodun to prepare image
      carousels and upload them as drafts to her own TikTok account. It is not offered to
      the public, has no user accounts, and is not used to process other people's data.
    </p>

    <h2>What it collects</h2>
    <p>When the operator connects her own TikTok account, the tool stores:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>an OAuth access token and refresh token for that account;</li>
      <li>the account's TikTok user identifier (<code>open_id</code>);</li>
      <li>the status of uploads it has made, so a draft is not sent twice.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      That is the complete list. The tool does not read the account's videos, followers,
      messages, analytics, or any other person's information. It requests only the
      permissions needed to upload a draft to the connected account.
    </p>

    <h2>What it does not collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No data about TikTok users other than the connected account holder.</li>
      <li>No advertising or tracking identifiers. The tool has no analytics.</li>
      <li>No payment information.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where it is stored</h2>
    <p>
      Tokens and upload records are held in a private Postgres database hosted by Supabase,
      reachable only with a server-side secret key. The images the tool uploads are stored
      in object storage and served from this domain, because TikTok downloads media from a
      verified URL rather than accepting a direct file upload for photo posts. Those images
      are content the operator created for publication and contain no personal data.
    </p>

    <h2>What is shared</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing is sold, and nothing is shared with third parties for their own purposes. Data
      moves only between the operator's own systems and TikTok's API in order to place a
      draft in the connected account.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      Tokens are kept only while the integration is in use and are replaced each time they
      are refreshed. The operator can revoke the app's access at any time from TikTok's own
      settings, which invalidates the stored tokens immediately; the stored copies are then
      deleted. To request deletion of anything held by this tool, use the contact address
      below.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If the tool's behaviour changes, this page is updated before the change ships, so that
      what is described here stays true of what the app actually does.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions or deletion requests: <a href="mailto:silkvoice1214@gmail.com">silkvoice1214@gmail.com</a></p>

    <p class="foot mono"><a href="/tiktok/terms">Terms of Service →</a></p>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 1.25rem 6rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    opacity: 0.6;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .legal h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.8rem); line-height: 1.1; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .updated { font-size: 0.78rem; opacity: 0.6; margin: 0 0 2.5rem; }
  .legal h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 2.2rem 0 0.6rem; }
  .legal ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  .legal li { margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .legal code { font-size: 0.9em; opacity: 0.85; }
  .foot { margin-top: 3rem; font-size: 0.82rem; }
</style>
